            "type": "text",
            "text": "Applies the doubling twice: 4λD / b = 48 mm"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      }
     ],
     "correct_key": "C",
     "explanation": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [],
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The angle of the first minimum is θ = λ / b = 600 × 10⁻⁹ / (0.10 × 10⁻³) = 6.0 × 10⁻³ rad. The distance from the centre to the first minimum = θD = 6.0 × 10⁻³ × 2.0 = 12 mm. The central maximum lies between the first minima on either side: 2 × 12 = 24 mm."
